1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,800
 Okay, now let's go on and take a look at Amazon Augmented AI.

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:10,000
 So you need to know about this service at a high level, so let me just give you an overview.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:19,260
 So Amazon Augmented AI or Amazon A21 is a service that makes it easy to build the workflow

4
00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:23,800
 required for human review of machine learning predictions.

5
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:29,800
 Now you can use human reviewers to step in when the model is unable to make a high

6
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:35,800
 confidence prediction or to audit its predictions on an ongoing basis.

7
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:38,500
 So now let me try and explain this through an example.

8
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:43,800
 So now let's say our model is trying to predict whether the image that is being shown

9
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:46,800
 is a cat or not.

10
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:52,100
 Now let's just assume that we showed the first image and it is able to predict that

11
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:56,100
 the image is a cat with 90% confidence.

12
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:57,300
 So that's good.

13
00:00:57,300 --> 00:01:04,500
 Now let's say we showed another image and it is able to predict that it is not a cat but

14
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:08,500
 with only 20% confidence level.

15
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:14,900
 So then what we can do is we can create a workflow where we say that if the model is able

16
00:01:14,900 --> 00:01:19,800
 to predict an image with a high confidence level, then we are good.

17
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:26,300
 But if it is not able to predict the image with a high confidence level, then that image

18
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:33,500
 can go to a human or a person to review the prediction of the model.

19
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:39,200
 So that is the key use case scenario for Amazon Augmented AI.

20
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:45,100
 So it provides built-in human review workflow for common machine learning use case.

21
00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:47,200
 And I think we just discussed that.

22
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:51,800
 So now let's take a real world use case on how it can be used.

23
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:59,700
 So it can be used in the insurance industry for insurance claims intake forms and prescriptions.

24
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:07,300
 So we can use Amazon text rack and implement human review of newest or sensitive data using

25
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:10,500
 Amazon AI 21.

26
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:16,700
 Then it can also be used for content moderation with Amazon Herak Commission.

27
00:02:16,700 --> 00:02:22,700
 So you can see a screenshot from Amazon Augmented AI and this should be shown to a human

28
00:02:22,700 --> 00:02:23,700
 reviewer.

29
00:02:23,700 --> 00:02:29,500
 So on the left side you have instructions on how you need to execute the task.

30
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:35,700
 So once the human reviewer looks at the instruction, then you can have Amazon text rack extract

31
00:02:35,700 --> 00:02:40,400
 the data from a handwritten note into this form.

32
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:46,800
 And then the human reviewer can mark the correctness of the data that has been imported

33
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:47,800
 on this side.

34
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:48,800
 Okay.

35
